# CardScout always requests live prices. Practice numbers appear only when that call fails.
# You do not set a demo mode here.

# Optional. A free key from https://dev.pokemontcg.io raises rate limits.
# How to get it:
# 1. Open https://dev.pokemontcg.io/ and create a key.
# 2. Paste it here.
# TCGPlayer is not granting new developer keys. CardScout reads the English raw
# market price from the Pokémon TCG API (tcgplayer.prices market/low/mid/high).
# The Values label is "TCGPlayer market (via Pokémon TCG API)".
# This key is optional. The API also works with this left blank.
POKEMONTCG_API_KEY=

# Required for graded slab prices. Paid PriceCharting subscription.
# How to get it:
# 1. Subscribe at https://www.pricecharting.com/
# 2. Open the subscription page → API/Download.
# 3. Copy the token. CardScout sends it as the `t` query parameter.
# Docs: https://www.pricecharting.com/api-documentation
# The API returns current grades only (PSA 10, BGS 10, and the other card columns).
# It does not return the history chart. The Values box links to that chart.
# Leave this blank and the PriceCharting box says it needs a key. No grades are invented.
PRICECHARTING_TOKEN=

# eBay client credentials from https://developer.ebay.com/ (Client ID and Client Secret).
# How to get them:
# 1. Create an application and a keyset.
# 2. Copy the Client ID and Client Secret (the Browse API client-credentials pair).
# 3. Ask eBay to allow Marketplace Insights for that app.
# Browse item_summary/search only returns active listings. It has no sold or
# completed filter, so CardScout does not use Buy It Now asks as sold prices.
# Sold search calls /buy/marketplace_insights/v1_beta/item_sales/search
# with scope https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/buy.marketplace.insights
# Leave the keys blank and the eBay box says Not configured. No sold prices are invented.
EBAY_CLIENT_ID=
EBAY_CLIENT_SECRET=
# PRODUCTION or SANDBOX. Defaults to PRODUCTION.
EBAY_ENV=PRODUCTION
